  "revision_notes": [
    "Seven changes were made after the lab was deleted and are not in the tested binary: a released copy frees its parts; a new stream takes a free cache index; a part is listed in a playlist only when its entry is recorded; an entry point assigns a new reader only to a cache with room for the bit rate of its playlist; the bit rate of a playlist is measured over at least four seconds; a new copy admits its first readers against the bit rate that the region advertises; an edge holds at most 15 playlists. They are covered by unit tests and the local lab.",
    "The default warm-up rate became 20 Mbit/s after the run. The run set it with a deploy setting."
  ],
  "source_material": {
    "video": "tos24-16m.ts: Tears of Steel, H.264 High 3840x2160, 24 fps, 16.5 Mbit/s, two-second closed GOP, sent without its audio track over RTMP from the London reader host",
