  "findings": [
    "A restarted cache was ignored by its parents because cache-mesh block identifiers restarted from the same value. Found in the local lab and corrected before the run.",
    "The HTTP/2 server did not set TCP_NODELAY. An 85 kB part took 42 ms to download. Corrected before the run with a newer web-services revision.",
    "Admission against the momentary bit rate of a playlist admitted a sixth 4K reader during a quiet passage. Found in the local lab and corrected before the run: admission uses the highest measured rate.",
    "Warming a 4K copy at 50 Mbit/s on a 1 vCPU edge delayed its audio readers by up to 1.2 s. The warm-up rate is now 20 Mbit/s.",
    "Caches number the segments of the 4K playlist differently when the key-frame interval is not the nominal segment length. Segment boundaries and program time agree.",
    "An edge kept about 500 MB of released 4K copies. Corrected after the run.",
    "Object-scaled cache-mesh symbols halve the processor use of an edge that serves 4K."
  ],
